      "writtenOn": "2026-11-27T07:53:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The loop only leaves early on name.absent (line 109) or on success. If Name is\npresent but Polarity is absent (UnknownProperty), or a property has the wrong\ntype (std::bad_variant_access, which lands in the std::exception catch at\nlines 51-53 with absent\u003dfalse), the loop retries every 2 s for the full 120 s\nand then fails with \"Incomplete mux configuration\". Neither case can recover.\n\nCould MuxProperty carry value / absent / transient, so that polarity.absent and\nnon-D-Bus exceptions fail immediately and only transient errors are retried?\ndbusGetRequiredProperty() in 97706 already treats std::exception as\nnon-transient, so the two should behave the same.",
      "revId": "8e1ef319d2147357c7b6b1b368362c73311877ab",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
